<title>CANADA: Canada Aug department store sales rise on month.</title>
<headline>Canada Aug department store sales rise on month.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian department stores sales rose a seasonally adjusted 1.2 percent in August from July to C$1.21 billion, Statistics Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>In unadjusted data, year-over-year sales in August rose 5.5 percent.</p>
<p>Sales at major stores rose 1.5 percent to C$526.6 million in August from the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>Consumer spending in the discount stores rose 8.9 percent to C$674.3 million from the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Mary Beth Garneau, Retail Trade Section, Industry Division, 613-951-9824.)</p>
<p>-- Ottawa Bureau 613 235-6745</p>
